# Project Agent Skills

- Cursor discovers **Agent Skills** from **`.cursor/skills/*/`** and **`.agents/skills/*/`** (each skill is a folder with `SKILL.md`; see [Cursor Skills](https://cursor.com/docs/context/skills)).
- This repo mirrors the same skills under **`.agents/skills/`** (symlinks → `.cursor/skills/`) so both discovery paths resolve.
- **Claude Code** discovers project skills from **`.claude/skills/*/`** (same `SKILL.md` format). This repo mirrors the same skills there too (symlinks → `.cursor/skills/`) so Cursor and Claude Code stay at parity.
- When the user’s task matches a skill’s **description** (e.g. `/keys/use-cases`, marketing flow diagrams, product-proof pages), **read that skill’s `SKILL.md` first** before large edits—do not rely on memory alone.
- **Before PRs** or when changes touch **keys, secrets, auth, encryption, Connect, MCP, gateway, or DB credentials**, read **restormel-high-risk-security** first ([docs/guides/pre-pr-security-review.md](../../docs/guides/pre-pr-security-review.md)).
- **Also read the matching skill first** for: **suite or module landings** (`/`, `/keys`, `/testing`, `/graph`), **`/integrations`**, **integration catalog or ecosystem strips**, **third-party logos** (`restormel-suite-integrations-marketing`, `restormel-third-party-brand-marks`, `restormel-integration-docs-hub`), **dashboard / Connect neu-brutalist UI** (`restormel-neu-brutalist-ui`), **service-admin reference pages** (`/keys/admin/**` — `restormel-admin-technical-writing`).
- For **large cross-route marketing or IA refactors**, prefer the **Task tool** (e.g. `explore`) to inventory affected routes before editing; keep edits narrow per [.cursor/rules/06-credit-efficiency.mdc](./06-credit-efficiency.mdc).
- New project skills: add under **`.cursor/skills/<kebab-name>/SKILL.md`**, set frontmatter **`name`** to match the folder name exactly, then add a matching symlink under **both** **`.agents/skills/`** and **`.claude/skills/`** (each `../../.cursor/skills/<kebab-name>`) so Cursor and Claude Code both discover it.
